 salt←CreateSalt length;⎕RL;alp
⍝ Returns a random salt of `length` characters, drawn from the ASCII letters `a-z` and `A-Z` and the digits `0-9`.
 ⎕RL←⍬ 2    ⍝ Use the operating system's random number generator: a seed derived from the time would make salts guessable
 alp←(⎕C ⎕A),⎕A,⎕D
 salt←alp[?length⍴≢alp]
